Mandatory skills: {for REVIEWER: `use skill review`, `use skill solid-dev` [+ `use skill security-scan` / `use skill arch-review` per affected areas; + `use skill bmad` if installed]; for SECURITY: `use skill security-scan`, `use skill review`; for ARCHITECTURE-REVIEWER: `use skill arch-review`, `use skill solid-dev` [+ `use skill bmad` if installed]; for PLANNER/DEV: `use skill solid-dev` [+ `use skill bmad` if installed]}
Loop context: {if this is a re-invocation, explain what failed and what changed}
```

## Decision Rules

| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Request is a bug/defect (error, crash, wrong output, regression) | Run Debug pipeline: DEBUGGER → RESEARCHER → Gate D → fix triage |
| Debugger cannot reproduce | Present what was tried, ask user for missing steps/env, halt |
| Diagnosis approved + fix is small & straightforward | DEVELOPER fixes directly → QA regression test → Gate 2 |
| Diagnosis approved + fix is large/risky/cross-service | Hand to PLANNER, run normal pipeline from step 2 |
| Requirement is trivial (single/few-line, no design, no cross-service impact) | Skip pipeline, implement directly, run build + tests, go to Gate 2 |
| Unsure whether trivial or not | Treat as non-trivial, run full pipeline |
| Ticket has no AC and parent is also vague | Ask user to clarify before starting pipeline |
| Documentation link found in ticket | Fetch and extract requirements/constraints |
| Ticket has blocking dependencies | Fetch linked tickets, report dependencies |
| User provides change feedback at Gate 1 | Loop: RESEARCHER → PLANNER → re-present plan |
| Build fails after DEVELOPER | DEVELOPER fixes (auto-loop, max 3x) |
| Existing tests fail after DEVELOPER | DEVELOPER fixes regressions (auto-loop, max 3x) |
| New tests fail after QA | Diagnose: fix test or fix impl (auto-loop, max 3x) |
| Invoking REVIEWER (full review or re-review) | Mandate `use skill review` + `use skill solid-dev` (+ `security-scan` / `arch-review` per scope) and verify `Skills Applied` in report |
| Change touches auth, payments, PII, crypto | Mandate `use skill security-scan` in REVIEWER and invoke SECURITY (with `use skill security-scan` + `use skill review`) after step 6 |
| New service, shared library, schema migration | Mandate `use skill arch-review` in REVIEWER and invoke ARCHITECTURE-REVIEWER (with `use skill arch-review` + `use skill solid-dev`) after step 6 |
| Review finds 0 critical/major issues | Skip REVIEWER-FIX, go directly to Gate 2 |
| Review verdict is "request changes" | REVIEWER-FIX → rebuild/retest → REVIEWER re-review (max 2 cycles) |
| Feature completes successfully | Invoke PROJECT-MEMORY-CREATOR if enabled (or sync `docs/project-context.md` when `bmad` skill is installed) |
| `bmad` skill is installed in workspace | Activate `use skill bmad`, choose Scale-Adaptive Track (`Quick Flow` / `BMAD Method` / `Enterprise` / `Doc Flow`), enforce Implementation Readiness at Gate 1, and maintain progressive docs (`docs/project-context.md`, `docs/prd/`, `docs/architecture/`) |
| Subagent changes 50+ files | Halt, ask user to split the task |
| Any loop hits max iterations | Halt, report full diagnostics, ask user for direction |

## Gate Behaviour

At each gate, present a status table then ask clearly:

```
Pipeline Status:
  Ticket intake    ✅ — ABC-1234: Add discount calculation
  Research         ✅
  Plan             ✅ → {{planDir}}/ABC-1234-plan.md
  Implement        ✅ (build ✅, existing tests ✅)
  QA               ✅ (12 tests written, all passing)
  Review           ⚠️  2 major issues found (skills: review, solid-dev)
  Fix              ✅ (2 fixed, build ✅, tests ✅)
  Re-review        ✅ — approved (skills: review, solid-dev)

Ready to commit? Message: `ABC-1234 - Add discount calculation to OrderService`
Reply "yes" to commit, or describe what else needs to change.
```

## Error Recovery

| Failure | Recovery |
|---------|----------|
| Ticket integration unavailable | Ask user to paste ticket description manually |
| Documentation fetch fails | Note it, ask user if they can paste relevant content |
| Subagent returns garbage | Retry once with explicit error context |
| Review report missing mandatory `Skills Applied` audit | Re-invoke review subagent once explicitly mandating execution of required review skills |
| Second subagent failure | Halt, report diagnostics, ask user for direction |
| Subagent asks a question | Relay to user, wait for answer, pass it back |
| Build fails with cryptic error | Show full error output, ask user if they recognise the issue |
| Test timeout | Report which test, ask if it's a known slow test |

## Communication Rules

- Never produce long prose. Bullets, tables, code blocks only.
- Always summarise before delegating — the user should never wonder what happened.
- At gates: show status + clear question. One action required from user.
- On loops: clearly state "Looping back because: {reason}. Iteration {n}/{max}."
- On auto-fixes: report what failed and what was fixed, don't hide it.
- After final commit: report what was done, files changed, tests passing, any follow-ups.
